        <h2 class="text-widget-title">Strict July 1 or 60-Day Window</h2>
        <p class="text-body-secondary pathway-item-desc">
          Appeals must be submitted to the county Board of Equalization (BOE) by July 1st or within 60 days of receiving your official Value Change Notice, whichever date is later.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento pathway-item-card">
        <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Legal Burden</div>
        <h2 class="text-widget-title">Overcoming Assessor Presumption</h2>
        <p class="text-body-secondary pathway-item-desc">
          The county assessor's valuation is presumed correct by law. Homeowners must present clear, cogent, and convincing evidence showing the assessment exceeds true fair market value.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento pathway-item-card">
        <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Evidence Quality</div>
        <h2 class="text-widget-title">Prior-Year Neighborhood Comps</h2>
        <p class="text-body-secondary pathway-item-desc">
          Strongest evidence relies on 3 to 5 arm's-length sales of similar homes in your immediate neighborhood that completed transactions prior to January 1st of the assessment year.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento pathway-item-card">
